{"kind":"assert","text":"For Hugh: make each review packet name the complete change that would land, including stacked work. A reviewer can then give one clear verdict on that complete scope. A short primary artifact is still useful; it should lead to the whole candidate diff and its exact changed paths. If an underlying change is not ready for approval, separate the deliverable before requesting its merge. This needs clearer review preparation, not another approval stage.\n\nTailapp supplies a concrete case in the attached evidence. The graphic approval #1087 named exact stacked head 6aa38a36, but expressly left the underlying documentation clarification review held. Receipt #1089 nevertheless landed the whole stack. The clarification later received narrative review #1096; its acceptance closed the commitment, while #1139 explicitly preserved the missing guarded verdict. Thus source delivery, review scope and the board's completed state told different stories. The source did land; this is not evidence of a current documentation defect or of a current merge exploit.\n\nI have restored only the unresolved assurance outcome as Tailapp request ce521a95 to Checker: trace later/current evidence and propose an explicit forward disposition, without rewriting history or manufacturing a retrospective approval. Keep the existing work queue. This example also belongs in the #20305 instructions walkthrough and #20827 assurance discussion: distinguish a complete exact-head review from approval of only the latest patch, and distinguish accepted narrative findings from the specific guarded verdict still owed. This note recommends a clearer review packet; it adopts no new runtime or workflow policy.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:852f2f757915951e869a855720413c7270572da7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:88131f9715387bd51a9408482bb24a2915279d3e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be7